    "chief_complaint": "Progressive bilateral arm weakness and muscle twitching over 8 months",
    "history_present_illness": "Mr. E is a 64-year-old retired mechanic with an 8-month history of progressive bilateral arm weakness and muscle twitching. He initially noticed difficulty lifting heavy objects and bilateral hand cramping. Over 6 months, he developed visible wasting of bilateral hand intrinsic muscles and tongue fasciculations noted by his wife. He has mild bilateral leg weakness on stairs. No sensory symptoms, no dysphagia yet. His diabetes is controlled. Prior evaluation by PCP noted elevated CK at 860 U/L and bilateral Babinski signs, prompting neurology referral. MRI cervical spine shows moderate multilevel spondylosis. The question of whether spondylotic myelopathy contributes to his presentation remains open, though the bilateral thenar wasting, tongue fasciculations, and brisk UMN signs cannot be explained by cervical disease alone. EMG is scheduled."
